///| cmd/proton_gui -- Loop #41: a native desktop shell for debugging the
///| client by hand, and Loop #41-M2's fault-injection console on top of it.
///|
///| Native-only by construction: Proton's manifest pins `preferred_target:
///| native` / `supported-targets: "+native"`, and the CEF runtime it drives
///| has no wasm story.  This package is the ONLY place in the module that
///| imports `@proton` -- `src/` must stay free of it so the 4-target KAT
///| gates never depend on a 0.x GUI framework.
///|
///| Everything protocol-shaped comes from `src/sftp`, the same package the
///| native TCP transport and the browser Worker transport drive.  The
///| console is a third *driver* of the one implementation, not a second
///| implementation: no byte assembly of its own, no parse rules of its own.
///|
///| `proton_contract` is imported for the command descriptors themselves.
///| It is not a GUI framework -- it is the transport-neutral
///| `Command[Request, Response]` value that `CommandRegistrar::bind`
/// registers, and it is what makes the route name (`app:<name>`) something
///| both sides derive rather than something either side hardcodes.
import {
  "moonbit-community/proton",
  "moonbit-community/proton_contract",
  "moonbitlang/async",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
  "openssh/openssh_moonbit/src/sftp",
}

pkgtype(kind: "executable")

// Proton is native-only (its manifest pins `supported-targets: "+native"`),
// and the compiler wants that stated here rather than inferred from the
// dependency -- which keeps a wasm check of this package a *declared*
// impossibility instead of a surprise.

options(
  supported_targets: "+native",
)
